; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8073  /****************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8074  /*  MISRA deviations                                                        */
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8075  /****************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8076  /* Justification for module-specific MISRA deviations:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8077  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8078  MD_CanIf_1.1:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8079    Reason: Complex code structure used and not split in modules or functions to make the code compact and efficient.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8080    Risk: Difficult to understand.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8081    Prevention: Code inspection and multiple configuration aspects used in component test.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8082  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8083  MD_CanIf_5.6:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8084    Reason: Same name is used for same kind of data
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8085    Risk: None.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8086    Prevention: None
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8087    
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8088  MD_CanIf_8.7:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8089    Reason: Definition of CanIfState in global section because of better over-view.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8090    Risk: Name conflict.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8091    Prevention: Compiler optimize and check for name conflicts.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8092  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8093  MD_CanIf_8.8_CanIf_Lcfg.c
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8094    Reason: Header files where the call back functions are defined are not known by CanIf.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8095    Risk: Compiler error occurs if a call back function with the same name is defined more than one time.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8096    Prevention: Configuration tool allows only to define a call back function with unique name otherwise an error occurs
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8097                during generation process.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8098  MD_CanIf_9.1:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8099    Reason: Variable is always set, the default case of the switch is not possible
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8100    Risk: Data access outside table.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8101    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different variants in the component test.  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8102  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8103  MD_CanIf_11.1:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8104    Reason: Cast to different pointer type required to avoid compiler warning due to usage of a union of function pointer types.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8105    Risk: None due to fact that function pointer are used.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8106    Prevention: Test of the different variants in the component test.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8107  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8108  MD_CanIf_11.5:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8109    Reason: Pointer cast to P2VAR is necessary to avoid compiler warning because "SduDataPtr" within "PduInfoType" is defined
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8110            as P2VAR during "CanSduPtr" is P2CONST.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8111    Risk: CAN data could be modified after cast to P2VAR.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8112    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different variants in the component test.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8113  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8114  MD_CanIf_13.7:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8115    Reason: Fullfills the AUTOSAR requirement to check the parameter against a valid value OR value and resulting logical operation may alternate depending on postbuild data
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8116    Risk: None.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8117    Prevention: None.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8118  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8119  MD_CanIf_14.1:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8120    Reason: Case1: This is the only one way to verify the size of Can_IdType.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8121            Case2: Statement is reachable if the function is called with illegal parameter.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8122            Case3: Statement is necessary to identify wrong generated data.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8123    Risk: None.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8124    Prevention: None.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8125  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8126  MD_CanIf_14.03:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8127    Reason: Empty statements occur multiple times because macros used like functions, and configuration aspects may deactivate complete functionality.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8128    Risk: Functionality is missing unexpectedly
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8129    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different variants in the component test.  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8130    
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8131  MD_CanIf_14.4:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8132    Reason: No default handling needed for if-else-if here.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8133    Risk: Missing default handling.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8134    Prevention: Code inspection.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8135  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8136  MD_CanIf_14.6:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8137    Reason: More than one break statement is used to terminate the loop during the search algorithm.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8138            This leads to more efficient code which is easier to read and maintain.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8139    Risk: Relevant fragments of code not executed.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8140    Prevention: Code inspection.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8141    
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8142  MD_CanIf_14.7
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8143    Reason: Multiple return paths used to optimize code (readability and runtime).
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8144    Risk: Return from a function too soon.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8145    Prevention: Code inspection.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8146    
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8147  MD_CanIf_16.4:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8148    Reason: AUTOSAR defines for each CanIf-upper-layer an own different name for function parameters. 
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8149            Due to support of different upper layers in parallel this violation can not avoided until AUTOSAR 
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8150            harmonizes the names of function parameters. 
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8151    Risk: The violation of this rule is not critical because only the names of parameters differ.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8152    Prevention: Test of software with real compiler and preprocessor on real MCU-target.  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8153    
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8154  MD_CanIf_19.10:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8155    Reason: Parameter used in structures that does not allow brackets.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8156    Risk: None atomic parameter lead to compile errors.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8157    Prevention: Used parameter is always atomic depend on usage.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8158    
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8159  MD_CanIf_19.13:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8160    Reason: Glue operator used to abstract AUTOSAR compiler abstraction
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8161    Risk: Only K&R compiler support glue operator
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8162    Prevention: Compile test show whether compiler accept glue operator
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8163  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8164  MD_CanIf_21.1:
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8165    Reason: In case the API is used in the right way then there is no any problem and thus the variable
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8166            which is used to access the array has not to be checked.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8167    Risk: API does not do what desired.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8168    Prevention: Use the API in the right way.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8169  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8170  MD_CanIf_1.1_NumberOfMacroDefinitions
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8171    Reason: Code which is much better / easier to maintain.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8172    Risk: Compiler and preprocessor do not support more than 1024 macro definitions
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8173    Prevention: Test of software with real compiler and preprocessor on real MCU-target.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8174  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8175  MD_CanIf_5.1
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8176    Reason: Code which is much better / easier to maintain.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8177    Risk: Compiler and preprocessor do not support identifiers with more than 31 characters.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8178    Prevention: Test of software with real compiler and preprocessor on real MCU-target.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8179  */
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8180  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8181  /* SBSW_JUSTIFICATION_BEGIN
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8182  
