; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8184  \DESCRIPTION Access to txPduDataWithChecksumPtr with index which is based on DLC
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8185  \COUNTERMEASURE \N Index is checked during runtime not to exceed the bounds of txPduDataWithChecksumPtr. Performed check: (PduInfoPtr->SduLength) > CANIF_CFG_MAXTXDLC_PLUS_DATACHECKSUM.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8186  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8187  \ID SBSW_CANIF_2
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8188  \DESCRIPTION Function call via function pointer. Function is read out of CanIf_DataChecksumRxErrFctPtr
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8189  \COUNTERMEASURE \S For the generated function declared by CanIf_DataChecksumRxErrFctPtr, it must be secured that a valid function callout is provided with valid signature. 
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8190                     Please see SMI-746 within the Safety Manual of the CAN interface.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8191                     The Callout function is optional, if no Callout is parametrized CanIf_DataChecksumRxErrFctPtr is defined as NULL_PTR, nothing to do.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8192  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8193  \ID SBSW_CANIF_3
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8194  \DESCRIPTION Access to CanIf_CtrlMode, CanIf_ChannelMode, CanIf_WakeUpValidationState, CanIf_PnWuTxPduFilterActive,
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8195               CanIf_TxConfState with index controlled by CANIF_CFG_MAX_CONTROLLER which is mapped to the CanIf_GetSizeOfCtrlStates()
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8196               which is provided by ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8197  \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL01/CSL03 of ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8198  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8199  \ID SBSW_CANIF_4
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8200  \DESCRIPTION Write access to dereferenced pointer ControllerModePtr
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8201  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The caller of the function CanIf_GetControllerMode must ensure that the pointer passed to the
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8202                     parameter ControllerModePtr is able to record a value of the type CanIf_ControllerModeType
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8203  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8204  \ID SBSW_CANIF_5
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8205  \DESCRIPTION Function call with referenced local variable/structure respectively passed-through parameter. 
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8206  \COUNTERMEASURE \N Pointer references stack variable and is therefor always valid. For passed-through datapointer the caller ensures that the 
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8207                     pointer is valid.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8208  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8209  \ID SBSW_CANIF_6   
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8210  \DESCRIPTION Access to CanIf_TxQueue via PduId which is  indirected over CanIf_TxPduQueueIndex.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8211  \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib. Pdu is passed through, caller ensures that PduId is valid.
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8212                     For API CanIf_CancelTxConfirmation() which is called from outside, the PduId is checked via CSL01 with reference value "CanIf_GetSizeOfTxPduConfig()".
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8213  
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8214  \ID SBSW_CANIF_7
; ..\BSW\CanIf\CanIf.c	  8215  \DESCRIPTION VStdMemCpy function call with parameter destination buffer pointer and length. 
